---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import { linuxPillars } from './linux-data';
import ConsoleMasthead from '../ConsoleMasthead.astro';
const topic = await getEntry('topics', 'linux');
if (!topic) throw new Error('Linux foundation topic metadata is missing.');
const date = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en', { year: 'numeric', month: 'short', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---

<article class="linux-hub" aria-labelledby="linux-hub-title" data-linux-hub>
  <ConsoleMasthead className="linux-topbar" brandClass="linux-brand" activeHref="/foundations" />
  <header class="linux-hub-head"><div><nav class="linux-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Library</a><span>/</span><a href="/foundations">Foundations</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Linux</span></nav><span class="linux-kicker">LINUX FOUNDATION · SYSTEM MAP</span><h1 id="linux-hub-title">One Linux machine. Eight lenses.</h1><p>Follow one web service through the primitives behind cloud, containers, and Kubernetes.</p></div><div class="linux-head-context"><span>REFERENCE HOST · devbox-01</span><span>FOUNDATIONAL · DEEP DIVE</span><span>Published {date.format(topic.data.published)} · Reviewed {date.format(topic.data.reviewed ?? topic.data.published)}</span></div></header>

  <section class="linux-map-section" aria-labelledby="linux-map-title"><div class="linux-map-heading"><div><span class="linux-kicker">THE MAP</span><h2 id="linux-map-title">Pick a subsystem to inspect.</h2></div><div class="linux-map-mode" role="group" aria-label="Map exploration mode"><button type="button" data-linux-mode="free" aria-pressed="true">Explore freely</button><button type="button" data-linux-mode="path" aria-pressed="false">Show suggested path</button></div></div>
    <div class="linux-map" data-map-mode="free" aria-label="Linux machine and eight pillar routes"><div class="linux-map-core"><span>DEVBOX-01</span><strong>LINUX MACHINE</strong><small>Userspace ↕ kernel ↕ hardware</small><a href="#linux-machine">Meet the machine ↓</a></div>{linuxPillars.map((pillar, index) => <a class={`linux-map-node linux-map-node-${pillar.id}`} href={`/linux/${pillar.id}`} aria-label={`Explore Linux ${pillar.name}`} data-linux-map-node={pillar.id}><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><strong>{pillar.name}</strong><small>{pillar.hints}</small><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>)}</div>
    <div class="linux-map-caption"><p data-linux-map-preview>One host, eight connected subsystems. Every lens opens a dedicated page; return here whenever you need the whole machine.</p><span>SELECT ANY NODE · NO LOCKED ORDER</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="linux-machine-basics" id="linux-machine" aria-labelledby="linux-machine-title"><div class="linux-basics-head"><span class="linux-kicker">ORIENTATION · DEVBOX-01</span><h2 id="linux-machine-title">Meet the Linux machine.</h2><p>Our reference web service runs as a process, reads configuration, opens a socket, and writes logs. Each pillar follows one of those relationships.</p></div><div class="linux-basic-layers" role="img" aria-label="Userspace processes call kernel services, which manage hardware"><div><span>USERSPACE</span><strong>shell · nginx · sshd</strong><small>Programs and operator tools</small></div><i aria-hidden="true">↕ system calls</i><div><span>KERNEL</span><strong>process · filesystem · network</strong><small>Resource and access decisions</small></div><i aria-hidden="true">↕ drivers</i><div><span>HARDWARE</span><strong>CPU · RAM · disk · NIC</strong><small>Physical or virtual devices</small></div></div><p class="linux-basics-caveat">Linux names the kernel and ecosystem; a distribution supplies userspace tools and configuration. This fixture uses a generic modern host, with systemd and distro-specific tools labelled in the pillar pages.</p>
    <div class="linux-orientation-pair"><div><h3>From boot to a service</h3><ol><li>Firmware</li><li>Bootloader</li><li>Kernel + initramfs</li><li>PID 1 / init system</li><li>Services and login</li></ol><p>systemd is common, not universal. A container does not normally run this full machine boot sequence.</p></div><div><h3>From / to a resource</h3><div class="linux-root-path"><code>/</code><span>etc · config</span><span>home · users</span><span>var · changing data/logs</span><span>proc / sys · virtual kernel views</span><span>dev · device entries</span></div><p>A pathname can cross a mount into another filesystem. Storage explores what backs it.</p></div></div></section>
  <footer class="linux-hub-bottom"><div><span class="linux-kicker">A SUGGESTED ROUTE, WHEN YOU WANT ONE</span><p>Identity → Storage → Processes → Networking → Packages → Shell → Security → Troubleshooting. Jump wherever your current question starts.</p></div><a href="/linux/identity">Start with Identity →</a><div class="linux-sitefoot"><span>Infra, Illustrated. · Linux foundations for cloud systems.</span><a href="/visualizations">Browse all visuals ↗</a></div></footer>
</article>

<script>
  for (const hub of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-linux-hub]')) {
    const map = hub.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.linux-map')!;
    const modeButtons = [...hub.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-linux-mode]')];
    modeButtons.forEach((button) => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const mode = button.dataset.linuxMode || 'free';
      map.dataset.mapMode = mode;
      modeButtons.forEach((other) => other.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(other === button)));
      hub.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-linux-map-preview]')!.textContent = mode === 'path' ? 'The numbered path is one way to build the primitives. Every pillar remains open for direct exploration.' : 'One host, eight connected subsystems. Every lens opens a dedicated page; return here whenever you need the whole machine.';
    }));
    hub.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-linux-map-node]').forEach((node) => {
      function preview() { const name = node.querySelector('strong')?.textContent || ''; const hints = node.querySelector('small')?.textContent || ''; hub.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-linux-map-preview]')!.textContent = `${name}: ${hints}. Open this dedicated console to follow the subsystem on devbox-01.`; }
      node.addEventListener('focus', preview); node.addEventListener('pointerenter', preview);
    });
  }
</script>
